ned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -5\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot (-5)-1\\cdot (-1))i-(1\\cdot (-5)-4\\cdot (-1))j+(1\\cdot 1-4\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =6i+j+5k \\\\  & =⟨6,1,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{62}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{62}}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe42615454e1c6e2a7cbc99f3504767cbeb3c62b1449110697dc7506cc85b93"} {"question" "q-127866" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "34ef4089e50c811a6505310afff18624d442c8f52325d9cc025eaba1e96da143"} {"question" "q-127866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe42615454e1c6e2a7cbc99f3504767cbeb3c62b1449110697dc7506cc85b93"} {"question" "q-127866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{13\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{31}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{62}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{31}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{62}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe42615454e1c6e2a7cbc99f3504767cbeb3c62b1449110697dc7506cc85b93"} {"question" "q-127866" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{62}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe42615454e1c6e2a7cbc99f3504767cbeb3c62b1449110697dc7506cc85b93"} {"question" "q-127915" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the $△\\,WXY,$ if $W(3,9,4),$ $X(1,7,3),$ $Y(6,12,8).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe42615454e1c6e2a7cbc99f3504767cbeb3c62b1449110697dc7506cc85b93"} {"question" "q-127915" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{WX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{WY}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{WX} & =x-w \\\\  & =(i+7j+3k)-(3i+9j+4k) \\\\  & =-2i-2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{WY} & =y-w \\\\  & =(6i+12j+8k)-(3i+9j+4k) \\\\  & =3i+3j+4k \\\\  & =⟨3,3,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{WX}\\times \\overset{\\to }{WY} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 4-3\\cdot (-1))i-((-2)\\cdot 4-3\\cdot (-1))j+((-2)\\cdot 3-3\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =-5i+5j \\\\  & =⟨-5,5,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{WX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{WY}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{WX}\\times \\overset{\\to }{WY}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+{5}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,WXY$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe42615454e1c6e2a7cbc99f3504767cbeb3c62b1449110697dc7506cc85b93"} {"question" "q-127915" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "34ef4089e50c811a6505310afff18624d442c8f52325d9cc025eaba1e96da143"} {"question" "q-127915" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe42615454e1c6e2a7cbc99f3504767cbeb3c62b1449110697dc7506cc85b93"} {"question" "q-127915" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe42615454e1c6e2a7cbc99f3504767cbeb3c62b1449110697dc7506cc85b93"} {"question" "q-127915" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe42615454e1c6e2a7cbc99f3504767cbeb3c62b1449110697dc7506cc85b93"} {"question" "q-275225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the length of the altitude $CH$ of the $△\\,ABC$, if $A(-2,0,-1)$, $B(0,-2,-1)$, $C(-3,-2,0).$\n\n$CH=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe42615454e1c6e2a7cbc99f3504767cbeb3c62b1449110697dc7506cc85b93"} {"question" "q-275225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the length of the altitude $CH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB\n$$\n\nSo, to find $CH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-2j-k)-(-2i-k) \\\\  & =2i-2j \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-3i-2j)-(-2i-k) \\\\  & =-i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 0)i-(2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 0)j+(2\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =-2i-2j-6k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-2,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{44} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{11}}{2}=\\sqrt{11}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $AB$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB \\\\ \\sqrt{11} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{11} & =CH\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{\\sqrt{22}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe42615454e1c6e2a7cbc99f3504767cbeb3c62b1449110697dc7506cc85b93"} {"question" "q-275225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "34ef4089e50c811a6505310afff18624d442c8f52325d9cc025eaba1e96da143"} {"question" "q-275225" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe42615454e1c6e2a7cbc99f3504767cbeb3c62b1449110697dc7506cc85b93"} {"question" "q-275225" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{22}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe42615454e1c6e2a7cbc99f3504767cbeb3c62b1449110697dc7506cc85b93"} {"question" "q-316409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the length of the altitude $IP$ of the $△\\,HIJ$, if $H(-1,2,0)$, $I(1,1,3)$, $J(0,-2,1).$\n\n$IP=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe42615454e1c6e2a7cbc99f3504767cbeb3c62b1449110697dc7506cc85b93"} {"question" "q-316409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that the length of the altitude $IP$ can be related to the area of $△\\,HIJ$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}IP\\cdot HJ\n$$\n\nSo, to find $IP,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{HJ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{HI}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{HJ} & =j-h \\\\  & =(-2j+k)-(-i+2j) \\\\  & =i-4j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,-4,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{HI} & =i-h \\\\  & =(i+j+3k)-(-i+2j) \\\\  & =2i-j+3k \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{HJ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{HI} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-4)\\cdot 3-1\\cdot (-1))i-(1\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 2)j+(1\\cdot (-1)-(-4)\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =-11i-j+7k \\\\  & =⟨-11,-1,7⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{HJ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{HI}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{HJ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{HI}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-11)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{7}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{171} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,HIJ$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{3\\sqrt{19}}{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $HJ$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}HJ & =|\\overset{\\to }{HJ}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}IP\\cdot HJ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}IP\\cdot HJ \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{19}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,IP\\cdot 3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{19} & =\\sqrt{2}\\,IP \\\\ IP & =\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{38}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe42615454e1c6e2a7cbc99f3504767cbeb3c62b1449110697dc7506cc85b93"} {"question" "q-316409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "34ef4089e50c811a6505310afff18624d442c8f52325d9cc025eaba1e96da143"} {"question" "q-316409" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe42615454e1c6e2a7cbc99f3504767cbeb3c62b1449110697dc7506cc85b93"} {"question" "q-316409" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{38}}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe42615454e1c6e2a7cbc99f3504767cbeb3c62b1449110697dc7506cc85b93"} {"question" "q-316530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the $△\\,STU,$ if $S(0,1,2),$ $T(2,3,1),$ $U(4,1,2).$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe42615454e1c6e2a7cbc99f3504767cbeb3c62b1449110697dc7506cc85b93"} {"question" "q-316530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{ST}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{SU}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ST} & =t-s \\\\  & =(2i+3j+k)-(j+2k) \\\\  & =2i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨2,2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{SU} & =u-s \\\\  & =(4i+j+2k)-(j+2k) \\\\  & =4i+0j+0k \\\\  & =⟨4,0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ST}\\times \\overset{\\to }{SU} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 0)i-(2\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 4)j+(2\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 4)k \\\\  & =0i-4j-8k \\\\  & =⟨0,-4,-8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{ST}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{SU}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{ST}\\times \\overset{\\to }{SU}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{80} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,STU$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{2}=2\\sqrt{5}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/state.json" "file_sha256" "fbe42615454e1c6e2a7cbc99f3504767cbeb3c62b1449110697dc7506cc85b93"} {"question" "q-316530" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14044786/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "34ef4089e50c811a6505310afff18624d442c8f52325d9cc025eaba1e96da143"} {"question" "q-316530" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/